PianoPolicy is new code for UniXNU-piano (BSD-2-Clause-Patent, LICENSE). Nothing is copied from anywhere. What it is based on:

UniXNU-piano (this repository), BSD-2-Clause-Patent:
  package/PianoKeyboard: its published properties (piano-keyboard-hall, -attached, -status, kIOMessageServicePropertyChange) and
    its piano-keyboard-lid mode (kIOPMDisableClamshell / kIOPMEnableClamshell, then kIOPMClamshellClosed / Opened), whose clamshell
    part this kext takes over. package/PianoThermal: its piano_thermal_state breadcrumb, readPowerSource (ExternalConnected) and
    gpuCeiling (callPlatformFunction on the class's service), Governor.h's Profile and profilePower (in the host test only).
    package/PianoA830: "piano-gpu-ceiling" (0 clears) and its slots (board/PianoGpuCeiling.h, piano-gpu-ceiling-clients).
    package/NativeGopDisplay: piano-display-power, its change messages, piano-display-power-messages. package/PianoBacklight: the service on IOPlatformExpertDevice with one thread
    woken by an IOLock event. patches/k27/0062: machdep.piano_sleep's format and the wake sources' rules.

Facts, read as references only (no code taken):
  xnu-12377 (k27, APSL 2.0; the kernel this runs on, built from this source): iokit/Kernel/IOPMrootDomain.cpp (setProperties and
    its 21 relayed PM settings, handlePowerNotification's clamshell, AC adaptor and sleep-now handling, shouldSleepOnClamshellClosed,
    requestUserActive's kIOPMMessageRequestUserActive without a display wrangler, sleepSystemOptions), RootDomainUserClient.cpp
    (its 21 methods), IOPMPowerSource.cpp (updateStatus's kIOPMMessageBatteryStatusHasChanged), iokit/IOKit/pwr_mgt/IOPM.h,
    IOPMPrivate.h, RootDomain.h, bsd/sys/sysctl.h and bsd/kern/kern_newsysctl.c (manual OIDs, the extensible machdep node,
    kernel_sysctlbyname), bsd/net/if_low_power_mode.c (an interface flag, not the system's Low Power Mode).
  macOS 26 on a Mac (binaries read for facts: strings, the cfstring references and the calls around them):
    /System/Library/CoreServices/powerd.bundle/powerd: Low Power Mode lives in its PMPowerModeHandler (the PM preference key
    LowPowerMode per power source, notify name com.apple.system.lowpowermode with its state, "LPM Active" in its own power-source
    dictionary); its kernel-facing calls (IORegistryEntrySetCFProperty, IOPMSetAggressiveness, IOPMSetSystemPowerSetting,
    sysctlbyname, IOServiceOpen of the root domain, AppleSmartBatteryManager and AppleSMC) carry no Low Power Mode key; the
    clamshell notify name com.apple.system.powermanagement.clamshellstate.
    IOKit.framework (dyld shared cache): IOPMFeatureIsAvailableWithSupportedTable decides "LowPowerMode" by the model
    (IOCopyModel: MacBookPro above 12, MacBookAir above 7, MacNN except 13,1-2 and 14,8), not by the kernel's Supported Features;
    IOPMSetEnergyModePreference goes to powerd over XPC.
  The Ubuntu project for piano (behaviour only): docs/ubuntu-history/device.md 2.2-2.3 (5 min idle suspend on battery, power key,
    HandleLidSwitchExternalPower=lock), kernel.md 2.3 and 2.9 (gpio95 rising only while blanked with the lid open, never gpio97,
    the lid wakes on opening only); docs/drivers/thermal.md 2, its Profiles row (Power Saver / Balanced caps, GPU 342 MHz).
